
export anchor Story_3bd34dfd267a2c18:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        The ribbon's Planning tab offers Draft Stories and Research, so either can
        be started without first opening the board and finding the Backlog's
        heading. Read these first:
        spec/ui/components/ribbon/planning-tab/index.pi#RibbonPlanningTab.groups,
        spec/ui/components/ribbon/planning-tab/index.pi#RibbonPlanningTab.commands,
        spec/ui/components/ribbon/index.pi#Ribbon.commands,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.creating,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.research,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.drafting,
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.keyboard and
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.paused.

        Once this is done:
        - RibbonPlanningTab has a second group, "Agent", after the "Plan" group.
          It holds two slim buttons that are not primary, so the collapsed ribbon
          leaves them out: "Draft Stories" with a sparkle icon, then "Research"
          with a magnifying-glass icon. Add both to RibbonPlanningTab.groups and
          RibbonPlanningTab.commands, written the way newStory and sendSprint are.
        - Clicking Draft Stories opens Planning, or selects its tab where it is
          already open. It then opens drafting in the side panel with the "Describe
          what you want" box focused, exactly as the Backlog heading's "Draft
          stories" button and Ctrl+Shift+D do (Planning.creating,
          Planning.drafting, Planning.keyboard).
        - Clicking Research does the same for research, with the "What should be
          looked into?" box focused, exactly as the Backlog heading's "Research"
          button and Ctrl+Shift+R do (Planning.research).
        - Each tooltip explains what the command does and gives its shortcut,
          Ctrl+Shift+D or Ctrl+Shift+R (Cmd on macOS), as Ribbon.commands
          requires.
        - Neither button is disabled while planning is paused. Drafting and
          research only change the plan, and a second research while paused keeps
          the pause (Planning.paused).
        - The ribbon's buttons and the Backlog heading's buttons share one route
          into the side panel, so there is no second copy of the open-and-focus
          behaviour.

        Update the spec first: RibbonPlanningTab gains the group and both
        commands, and Planning.creating and Planning.research say that the ribbon's
        Planning tab offers them too. Then change the ribbon code to match.
        \\\

    mode: combined

    model: opus
